invariant: INV-42
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: rsa_sign_test_host
reason: rsa_sign64_key_ok computes the product of the primes and admits
  the key whatever it is. A key whose p or q is not a factor of its
  modulus then passes ch_srv_check's key test, and the arithmetic runs
  under a modulus record built for a number that may be even or short.
  The signature's check still refuses what comes out, so no vector
  notices. bin/rsa_sign_test_host changes one bit of p and requires the
  key test to refuse the key.

--- old
    return differ == 0;
--- new
    (void)differ;
    return 1;
